1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-0--0e-where-to-begin","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-0/0e-where-to-begin","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-0/0e-where-to-begin","sourceHash":"5c5bec1d2956f199deafacca1346cff033ba71edef0fdbf4c60ec6784e4ba52d","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:35.395Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"0E — Where to Begin","zh":"0E — 从哪里开始"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"where-should-you-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Where Should You Start?","zh":"你应该从哪里开始？"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Refold Method is written as if you're learning from absolute zero — like you just decided, today, to learn German or Swahili or whatever. That's just the most logical way to organize the information.","zh":"Refold 方法的写法，假设你是从绝对零基础开始学习——比如你今天刚决定学习德语、斯瓦希里语，或其他任何语言。这只是组织信息最合乎逻辑的方式。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"But most people who come across this method <em>aren't</em> absolute beginners. Maybe you've had years of classes, or you're living in the country, or you have a 2000-day streak on Duolingo.","zh":"但大多数接触到这一方法的人<em>并不是</em>绝对初学者。也许你已经上了多年的课，也许你正住在目标语言所在的国家，或者你在 Duolingo 上已经连续学习了 2000 天。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This article is here to help you figure out where in the process you should start, so you don't waste your time.","zh":"本文旨在帮助你判断应该从学习过程中的哪个阶段开始，从而避免浪费时间。"}},{"id":"total-beginner","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Total Beginner","zh":"完全初学者"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're a total beginner, you can skip the rest of this article and move on to <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1\">Phase 1: Foundations</a>.","zh":"如果你是完全初学者，可以跳过本文其余部分，直接进入<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1\">第 1 阶段：基础</a>。"}},{"id":"false-beginner","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"False Beginner","zh":"伪初学者"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"A \"false beginner\" is someone who has taken classes in school or has been learning on an app for a few months, but still can't really understand anything in the language.","zh":"“伪初学者”指的是在学校上过课，或在应用程序上学习了几个月，但仍然几乎无法理解这门语言的人。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is where the vast majority of language learners in the world end up. There's nothing wrong with being a false beginner — everyone on the Refold team has been one.","zh":"世界上绝大多数语言学习者最终都处于这个阶段。成为伪初学者没有任何问题——Refold 团队中的每个人都曾经是伪初学者。"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you know a bit <em>about</em> your target language but can't understand more than basic sentences, you're a false beginner. Start with <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1\">Phase 1: Foundations</a>, but you can either skip or skim Phase 1A.","zh":"如果你对目标语言<em>有一些了解</em>，但无法理解超出基础句子的内容，那么你就是伪初学者。从<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1\">第 1 阶段：基础</a>开始，但可以跳过或快速浏览第 1A 阶段。"}},{"id":"heritage-speaker","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Heritage Speaker","zh":"传承语使用者"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're here to learn the native language of your parents or grandparents, you're a heritage speaker. If you grew up hearing the language at home and picked up a lot of it naturally, you have a huge head start.","zh":"如果你来这里是为了学习父母或祖父母的母语，那么你属于传承语使用者。如果你从小在家里听着这门语言长大，并自然地掌握了很多内容，那么你已经拥有巨大的领先优势。"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"A common challenge for heritage speakers is that, while they often have very good pronunciation and listening skills, they have a limited vocabulary and little knowledge of the written language. This is especially true if the language has a very different writing system — for example, someone growing up in the United States with Mandarin-speaking parents.","zh":"传承语使用者常见的挑战是：虽然他们通常拥有很好的发音和听力技能，但词汇量有限，对书面语言也了解不多。如果这门语言的书写系统与他们熟悉的系统差异很大，这种情况尤其明显——例如，一个在美国长大、父母说普通话的人。"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're a heritage speaker, it's still a good idea to start with <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1\">Phase 1: Foundations</a> and work through the phases in order, but you'll complete them much faster — potentially in half or a third of the time it takes a total beginner.","zh":"如果你是传承语使用者，仍然建议从<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1\">第 1 阶段：基础</a>开始，并按顺序完成各个阶段，但你的完成速度会快得多——所需时间可能只有完全初学者的一半甚至三分之一。"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Phase 1 focuses on <em>how</em> to learn. Phase 2 is about building up comprehension skills, which you may already partly have. Phases 3 and 4 you'll probably find pretty easy. Once you get to Phase 5 and beyond, things will even out and you'll be in more or less the same boat as other learners.","zh":"第 1 阶段重点讲解<em>如何</em>学习。第 2 阶段讲的是培养理解能力，而你可能已经具备其中一部分。第 3 和第 4 阶段对你来说可能会相当容易。到了第 5 阶段及以后，你的情况会逐渐与其他学习者趋于一致，基本上会处于相似的起点。"}},{"id":"upper-beginner","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Upper Beginner","zh":"初级进阶"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you've been taking classes or learning for a while, you might be an upper beginner. You can read simple texts and understand basic conversation — maybe even hold a simple conversation yourself. You probably know 1,000–2,000 words and have a grasp of the basic grammar.","zh":"如果你已经上课或学习了一段时间，可能属于初级进阶水平。你能阅读简单文本，理解基础对话，甚至可能自己进行简单交流。你大概掌握了 1000–2000 个词，也了解基础语法。"}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your best starting point is <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2b-develop-your-comprehension\">2B — Develop your Comprehension</a>, but take a quick detour through <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1/1b-effort-tracking\">1B — Effort Tracking</a> first. Phase 1B covers ideas that are very helpful for the method as a whole. You could just read it, then jump right to 2B.","zh":"最适合你的起点是<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2b-develop-your-comprehension\">2B — 培养理解能力</a>，但先快速浏览一下<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1/1b-effort-tracking\">1B — 跟踪学习投入</a>。第 1B 阶段介绍的理念对整个方法都很有帮助。你可以读完这一阶段，然后直接跳到 2B。"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Some upper beginners prefer starting from Phase 1A and working through it quickly, just to get a refresher on the basics and make sure everything is fresh. If you haven't studied the language in a few years, that's probably the best option for you.","zh":"一些初级进阶学习者更喜欢从第 1A 阶段开始并快速完成，以便复习基础知识，确保一切都保持熟悉。如果你已经有几年没有学习这门语言了，这可能是最适合你的选择。"}},{"id":"returning-learner","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Returning Learner","zh":"重新开始学习者"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Maybe you used to be pretty decent at the language — you studied it for years, or spent time living abroad — but then life happened. You stopped using it, and now, years later, you've forgotten a lot.","zh":"也许你过去曾经相当擅长这门语言——学习了很多年，或曾在国外生活过——但后来生活发生了变化。你停止使用它，多年之后已经忘记了很多。"}},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The good news is that reactivating a language is significantly faster than learning one from scratch. A lot of what you learned is still in there, just buried. Immersion tends to bring it back surprisingly quickly.","zh":"好消息是，重新激活一门语言要比从头学习快得多。你学过的很多内容仍然存在，只是被暂时埋藏起来了。沉浸往往能以惊人的速度将它们重新唤回。"}},{"id":"segment-0023","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're not sure where you stand anymore, try watching a TV show or reading a short article in the language. If you can follow the gist with some effort, start at <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2b-develop-your-comprehension\">2B — Develop your Comprehension</a> or <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2c-solidify-your-reading\">2C — Solidify your Reading</a>. If it feels like starting over, treat yourself as a false beginner or upper beginner (above) and start earlier. You'll move fast either way.","zh":"如果你不确定自己现在处于什么水平，可以尝试用这门语言观看一集电视节目或阅读一篇短文。如果你稍加努力就能跟上大意，可以从<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2b-develop-your-comprehension\">2B — 培养理解能力</a>或<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2c-solidify-your-reading\">2C — 巩固阅读能力</a>开始。如果感觉像是重新开始，就把自己当作伪初学者或初级进阶学习者（见上文），从更早的阶段开始。无论哪种情况，你都会进步得很快。"}},{"id":"intermediate","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Intermediate","zh":"中级"}},{"id":"segment-0025","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you can read easy books, watch YouTube videos and <em>mostly</em> understand what's being said, you're probably intermediate. You may also be able to have a decent conversation or write text messages in the language.","zh":"如果你能阅读简单的书籍、观看 YouTube 视频，并且<em>大致</em>理解其中所说的内容，那么你可能处于中级水平。你也许还能进行不错的对话，或用这门语言发送短信。"}},{"id":"segment-0026","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"But that's about it. Intermediate learners struggle with depth. Fast movies or TV shows are hard. When two or three native speakers talk to each other, you're totally lost.","zh":"但基本也就到此为止。中级学习者在理解深度方面会遇到困难。快速的电影或电视节目很难理解。当两三个母语者互相交谈时，你会完全听不懂。"}},{"id":"segment-0027","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If this is you, it's probably best to jump into <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2c-solidify-your-reading\">2C — Solidify your Reading</a>, or even skip straight to <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-3/3a-overcome-the-listening-gap\">3A — Overcome the Listening Gap</a>. I'd recommend starting with 2C just while you learn how to learn with the Refold method, then move on to 3A after a few dozen hours.","zh":"如果你属于这种情况，最好直接进入<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2c-solidify-your-reading\">2C — 巩固阅读能力</a>，甚至直接跳到<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-3/3a-overcome-the-listening-gap\">3A — 克服听力差距</a>。我建议先从 2C 开始，用几十个小时熟悉如何使用 Refold 方法学习，然后再进入 3A。"}},{"id":"segment-0028","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You should also read through <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1/1b-effort-tracking\">1B — Effort Tracking</a>, since it covers ideas that are useful for the method as a whole. But don't start there.","zh":"你还应该阅读<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-1/1b-effort-tracking\">1B — 跟踪学习投入</a>，因为其中介绍的理念对整个方法都很有用。但不要从这里开始。"}},{"id":"advanced","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Advanced","zh":"高级"}},{"id":"segment-0030","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you already know several thousand words and have been learning for a while, but want to brush up and take things further, there are a lot of places you could start.","zh":"如果你已经掌握了几千个词，并且学习了一段时间，但想复习巩固并进一步提升，那么有很多地方可以作为起点。"}},{"id":"segment-0031","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You'll probably benefit from the techniques and resources across all the phases, but you don't need to do them in order. Depending on what you want to focus on:","zh":"你可能会从所有阶段的技巧和资源中受益，但不必按顺序完成。根据你想重点提升的方面："}},{"id":"segment-0032","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Want to improve your reading and ability to understand native content? Jump into <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2c-solidify-your-reading\">2C — Solidify your Reading</a>.","zh":"想提高阅读能力，以及理解母语内容的能力？直接进入<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2/2c-solidify-your-reading\">2C — 巩固阅读能力</a>。"},{"en":"Need to work on your listening since natives talk so fast? Start at <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-3/3b-choosing-a-dialect\">3B — Choosing a Dialect</a> or <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-3/3c-core-listening-skills\">3C — Core Listening Skills</a>.","zh":"需要加强听力，因为母语者说话太快？从<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-3/3b-choosing-a-dialect\">3B — 选择方言</a>或<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-3/3c-core-listening-skills\">3C — 核心听力技能</a>开始。"},{"en":"Want to practice your speaking? Any of the sub-phases in <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-4\">Phase 4: Speaking</a> would work.","zh":"想练习口语？<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-4\">第 4 阶段：口语</a>中的任何一个子阶段都可以。"},{"en":"Need to improve your writing? <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-5/5a-writing-comfort\">5A — Writing Comfort</a> makes the most sense.","zh":"需要提高写作能力？<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-5/5a-writing-comfort\">5A — 提升写作熟练度</a>最适合。"}]},{"id":"segment-0033","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Once you finish a phase, you can jump to a different one or just keep going forward chronologically.","zh":"完成一个阶段后，你可以跳到另一个阶段，也可以按时间顺序继续向前。"}},{"id":"very-advanced","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Very Advanced","zh":"非常高级"}},{"id":"segment-0035","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're already a high-level user of the language but want to use the Refold method to improve your study habits and pick up more useful techniques, it's going to be hard for me to point you to one specific place.","zh":"如果你已经是这门语言的高水平使用者，但想通过 Refold 方法改进学习习惯，并掌握更多实用技巧，那么我很难为你指出一个具体的起点。"}},{"id":"segment-0036","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The best thing for you would probably be to read through the entire roadmap and then take whatever seems valuable and put it into your own routine. You might like some of the foundational activities taught in <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2\">Phase 2: Comprehension</a>, or the more specialized ones in <a href=\"/roadmap/phase-7\">Phase 7: And Beyond</a>. Browse, experiment, and take what works.","zh":"对你来说，最好的做法可能是通读整份路线图，然后挑选有价值的内容，融入自己的日常学习安排。你可能会喜欢<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-2\">第 2 阶段：理解能力</a>中介绍的一些基础活动，也可能更需要<a href=\"/roadmap/phase-7\">第 7 阶段：以及更进一步</a>中的专业活动。浏览、尝试，然后采用适合你的内容。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
